_hist":null,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":0.19641783530882528,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":98.2,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.029936031155613396,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":95.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.008200694460627708,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":13.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.08229782196252566,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":60.8,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.04951571673153443,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":49.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.006549255852995395,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":18.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0153946937438585,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":74.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.01181,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"UL Solutions Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides testing, inspection and certification services and related software and advisory services worldwide. It operates through three segments: Industrial, Consumer, and Software and Advisory. The Industrial segment provides testing, inspection, and certification services across various end markets, including energy, industrial automation, engineered materials, and built environment, as well as stakeholders, such as manufacturers, building and asset owners, end users, and regulators. The Consumer segment offers safety certification testing, ongoing certification, global market access, testing for connectivity, performance and quality, and critical systems advisory and training services, as well as product market acceptance and risk mitigation services for customers in the consumer products end markets comprising consumer electronics, medical devices, information technologies, appliances, HVAC, lighting, and retail, as well as consumer applications, such as new mobility, smart products, and 5G. The Software and Advisory segment provide software and technical advisory services that enable customers to manage regulatory requirements, deliver supply chain transparency, and operationalize sustainability. It offers ULTRUS, a software that helps customers meet regulatory, supply chain, and sustainability challenges. UL Solutions Inc. was formerly known as UL Inc. and changed its name to UL Solutions Inc. in December 2021. The company was founded in 1894 and is headquartered in Northbrook, Illinois. UL Solutions Inc. operates as a subsidiary of ULSE Inc.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Jennifer F. Scanlon | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $7.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $209K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $28K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 38\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["UL Solutions Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $15.9B market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $403M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.85\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 41% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.40841489916922813},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"7,620 Shares of UL Solutions Inc. $ULS Purchased by Oppenheimer & Co. Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/7620-shares-of-ul-solutions-inc-uls-purchased-by-oppenheimer-co-inc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793958329.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.926,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (ULS)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_ULS_110626042601_1793957161.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793957161.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"UL Solutions (NYSE:ULS) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Meets Estimates","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/ul-solutions-nyseuls-posts-quarterly-earnings-results-meets-estimates.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793905019.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"UL Solutions (NYSE:ULS) CEO Sells $937,875.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/ul-solutions-nyseuls-ceo-sells-937875-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-04","times